# TensorFold Integration Proposal for ODS

**Experimental track:** `ods-evolution`  
**Project:** LEONES  
**Date:** 2026-10-11  
**Status:** Architecture and integration study — aligned with the inference-engines plan; ready for ODS scaffold after review  
**Upstream:** https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold — https://tensorfold.dev  
**License:** Apache-2.0 (from 0.6.0; earlier releases MIT)  
**Master plan:** `docs/integrations/PLAN-INTEGRACION-MOTORES-INFERENCIA-ODS.md`

---

## 1. Executive summary

**TensorFold** is an open-source local inference engine aimed at **specific model families**. It provides:

- Family-written kernels (Metal / CUDA).
- Speculative decoding with a **byte-identical exactness** contract relative to serial decoding on the **same** engine, weights, and settings.
- OpenAI-compatible API (chat/completions, completions, responses) and Anthropic Messages.
- Native Zig runtime (1.0.x): serve without Python or MLX installed on the host.
- Qualified checkpoints (MLX affine and project-owned recipes); it is **not** a generic GGUF loader.

The appropriate role in ODS is:

> **optional specialized (family-specific) runtime**, selected only when hardware and family/checkpoint appear in TensorFold’s qualified matrix.

It must **complement, not replace**, upstream ODS `llama-server`. It is complementary to **cafe-llama.cpp** (advanced llama.cpp drop-in) and **Strata** (extreme placement for Flash Next on consumer GPUs).

---

## 2. Why it fits LEONES → ODS

ODS already has `llama-server` as the core runtime and cafe-llama as an advanced compatible candidate. TensorFold adds a different dimension:

| Aspect | llama-server | cafe-llama.cpp | TensorFold |
|--------|--------------|----------------|------------|
| Model scope | Broad GGUF | Broad GGUF + safetensors | Short family-specific list |
| OpenAI API | Yes | Yes | Yes (+ Anthropic Messages) |
| Speculative | Partial | MTP / n-gram / PLE | MTP / DFlash + **exact same-engine** |
| Checkpoint format | GGUF | GGUF + native safetensors | MLX affine / TensorFold-owned |
| Kernels | General ggml | Extensions on llama.cpp | Per family (Metal/CUDA) |
| Output contract | None formal | None formal | Drafted == serial (byte-identical) |
| Install | Container / native | Multi-arch binaries | Native Zig 1.0.x (preferred); Python 0.6 fallback |

It fits **Inference Configuration Discovery (ICD)**:

```text
hardware + family + qualified checkpoint + draft + workload
        ↓
   Measured Inference Profile (only MEASURED asserts local performance)
```

This lets ODS offer high-throughput, reproducible-exact paths where TensorFold is qualified, without replacing the generic GGUF path.

