## 3. Key TensorFold capabilities (1.0.x status)

### 3.1 Native Zig runtime (1.0.x)

- Serve without Python or MLX in the serving process.
- Checkpoint load, tokenization, chat templates, and inference in the native binary.
- Python 0.6 line retained for families/paths not yet on native.

### 3.2 Exact speculative decoding

- A drafter proposes tokens; the target model verifies them in batch.
- Only tokens that match serial decoding on the **same** engine are accepted.
- Releases document drafted == serial checks.
- **Important for LEONES:** this is an *intra-engine* contract, not equivalence between TensorFold and llama.cpp / vLLM / others.

### 3.3 Orientative qualified matrix (1.0.4 — update with each release)

| Family / model | Checkpoint format | Qualified platform (documented) | Draft |
|----------------|-------------------|----------------------------------|-------|
| Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B-A3B | MLX affine 4-bit + MTP head | Metal M1–M5; CUDA GB10 / RTX 3090 | Included MTP |
| Qwen3.8-27B | MLX affine 4-bit + DFlash2 | Metal M5 Max, M3 Ultra | DFlash2 |
| Qwen3.8 Flash Next | MLX affine 6-bit (or other recipes) | Metal M5 Ultra (and CUDA paths in Python line/recipes) | MTP |
| GLM-5.3-Flash | MLX affine 4-bit | Metal dual M5 Ultra; multi-rank CUDA in recipes | MTP / DFlash2 |
| Qwen3.5-2B | MLX affine 4-bit | Metal M5 Max | — |

This table is **OBSERVED** from TensorFold releases and README. It does not imply support on unlisted hardware (e.g. RTX 3050 4 GB) until local MEASURED evidence exists.

### 3.4 API and operations

- OpenAI: `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/completions`, `/v1/responses`, `/v1/models`.
- Anthropic Messages.
- Health, metrics, dashboard options per release.
- Commands: `tensorfold serve`, `pull`, `models`, `info`, `capabilities`.

### 3.5 Typical install

```bash
# macOS (Homebrew)
brew install ashhart/tensorfold/tensorfold

# or install script
curl -fsSL https://tensorfold.dev/install.sh | sh

# serve (conceptual example)
tensorfold serve "$HOME/models/nemotron-lightning" \
  --name local-model --parallel 1 --context 8192 --temperature 0
```

Client base URL: `http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1` (engine default; in ODS it sits behind the unified proxy).

