## 7. Recommended implementation phases

Aligned with `PLAN-INTEGRACION-MOTORES-INFERENCIA-ODS.md` and the cafe-llama pattern.

### Phase 1 — Documentation and registry (this document in LEONES)

- Updated integration proposal (this file).
- Runtime Registry / ROADMAP entry.
- Versioned qualified matrix (source: TensorFold releases).

### Phase 2 — Optional runtime in ODS (PR to Osmantic/ODS or working fork)

- Opt-in `tensorfold` service (`extensions/services/tensorfold/`).
- Native-first install + health + `ods status`.
- Priority parameters in Dashboard → Models (advanced).
- Unified OpenAI-compatible proxy.

### Phase 3 — ICD profiles

- Predefined profiles only for qualified combinations (e.g. “Nemotron Lightning exact-MTP”, “Qwen3.8-27B DFlash2 Metal”).
- Candidate generation → local benchmark → best profile.
- Explicit fallback to cafe-llama / llama-server.

### Phase 4 — MEASURED evidence

- Standard workloads (tok/s, TTFT, peak memory, drafted==serial check).
- Side-by-side comparison only when the same workload is runnable on another runtime (without forcing output equivalence).
- Persist measured Inference Profiles.

---

## 8. What not to do

- Do not replace default ODS `llama-server`.
- Do not present TensorFold as a generic backend or as “best at everything”.
- Do not serve arbitrary ODS GGUF catalog models through TensorFold.
- Do not copy DGX Spark / M5 Mac benchmarks as `MEASURED` on different hardware.
- Do not treat “exact same-engine” as cross-runtime equivalence.
- Do not claim AMD / native Windows / low-VRAM RTX support without MEASURED validation.
- Do not mix TensorFold checkpoint caches with the GGUF catalog.
- Do not open an implementation PR against Osmantic/ODS without design review in LEONES.

---

## 9. Relationship with cafe-llama, Strata, and AirLLM

| Runtime | Main strength | Integration type |
|---------|---------------|------------------|
| llama-server | Broad, stable baseline | Core |
| cafe-llama.cpp | MoE offload + Turbo KV + generic MTP | Advanced **compatible** runtime (GGUF) |
| **TensorFold** | Family kernels + exact speculative | **Specialized** family-specific runtime |
| Strata | Flash Next on 12–24 GB (multi-tier placement) | Memory/placement runtime |
| AirLLM | Layer streaming; minimal VRAM | Experimental; not production |

Cafe and TensorFold are **complementary**: Cafe expands llama.cpp configurations; TensorFold offers closed engines with an exactness contract and speed on qualified families. Strata covers the “Flash Next on a gaming PC” extreme. AirLLM is research-only.

